WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.081 --> 00:00:02.212
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom.

00:00:02.212 --> 00:00:04.932
Tonight we're drinking
some very light white wine

00:00:04.932 --> 00:00:08.620
because I just ate my
weight in Chinese food.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.284
So, cheers.

00:00:10.284 --> 00:00:12.651
Now, I know a lot of you
guys watch this series

00:00:12.651 --> 00:00:14.187
while you're drinking a glass of wine.

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:16.840
You wait til Saturday evening,
you pour yourself a glass,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:17.673
and you watch this.

00:00:17.673 --> 00:00:18.679
So you guys are the best.

00:00:18.679 --> 00:00:20.643
You're my favorite wine drinking buddies.

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:23.264
Let's talk about the worst
people to drink wine with.

00:00:23.264 --> 00:00:24.734
So first, the know-it-all.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:27.359
There's always this one person
who you're drinking wine with

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:30.498
and they're like, oh, you
know, this bottle was harvested

00:00:30.498 --> 00:00:33.446
in the nether regions of Netherland.

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:36.429
They harvested the grapes
at the peak of winter

00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:38.689
so you can taste the
huckleberries that were growing

00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:39.826
in the ground.

00:00:39.826 --> 00:00:41.332
(crickets)

00:00:41.332 --> 00:00:43.939
I don't care where it's from,
I don't care who made it,

00:00:43.939 --> 00:00:45.449
I don't care how old it was.

00:00:45.449 --> 00:00:49.616
I have three questions for
you when we are drinking wine.

00:00:56.354 --> 00:00:59.285
My only exception to wine
experts is Chris Webb,

00:00:59.285 --> 00:01:01.776
our friendly neighborhood sommelier.

00:01:01.776 --> 00:01:04.586
He's the best, he's amazing,
he brings several bottles

00:01:04.586 --> 00:01:07.892
of wine, and I can sip them
while I'm listening to him talk.

00:01:07.892 --> 00:01:09.520
Next, wine snobs.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:10.998
These are different from experts.

00:01:10.998 --> 00:01:13.013
They're almost worse than experts.

00:01:13.013 --> 00:01:15.573
But there's always this
person who will invite you

00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:17.528
to a party, it's usually a dinner party,

00:01:17.528 --> 00:01:18.663
and you'll bring a bottle of wine

00:01:18.663 --> 00:01:20.528
and they're the biggest
fucking snob about it.

00:01:20.528 --> 00:01:24.983
They're like, oh, I only
drink Bordeauxs crafted

00:01:24.983 --> 00:01:28.733
in the 1800s, sorry,
this is like a 1940, eh.

00:01:29.944 --> 00:01:32.137
And then, if they try
the wine that you brought

00:01:32.137 --> 00:01:35.981
that's subpar, they make the
biggest fucking deal out of it.

00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:38.155
Like, they'll be holding the wine like,

00:01:38.155 --> 00:01:42.832
I can't believe I'm drinking
this, I never drink.

00:01:42.832 --> 00:01:43.665
Agh, uh.

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:46.471
It's like, stop ruining everyone's time

00:01:46.471 --> 00:01:48.243
with your assholishness.

00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.885
Wine all tastes the same.

00:01:49.885 --> 00:01:52.781
I think we can all agree
that wine tastes the same.

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:55.860
So to all you wine snobs out
there, I'm calling you out.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:57.564
I know it all tastes the same,

00:01:57.564 --> 00:02:00.006
and I know you know it
all tastes the same.

00:02:00.006 --> 00:02:01.423
So stop frontin'.

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:04.223
♫ I just do what I do

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.056
♫ You see me?

00:02:05.056 --> 00:02:07.381
♫ I just do what I do

00:02:07.381 --> 00:02:10.065
Next, the people who think that
since you're drinking wine,

00:02:10.065 --> 00:02:13.189
you have to talk about the
most boring stuff ever.

00:02:13.189 --> 00:02:15.458
Whenever I'm drinking
with a group of adults,

00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:17.783
all of a sudden they think
that since we're drinking wine,

00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:20.308
the following topics are
the most fascinating things

00:02:20.308 --> 00:02:21.567
on the planet.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:25.821
Gardening, staycations, SoulCycle,
Downton Abbey, meal prep.

00:02:25.821 --> 00:02:29.182
Oh, I tried the best Blue
Apron recipe yesterday,

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:30.869
it was a Thai chicken burger.

00:02:30.869 --> 00:02:33.373
And it came with a lemon
already cut, and it was so nice.

00:02:33.373 --> 00:02:35.242
And then I had leftovers for the next day.

00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:36.888
Is there anything better than meal prep?

00:02:36.888 --> 00:02:38.388
Ugh, I don't care.

00:02:39.429 --> 00:02:40.635
When we're drinking wine,

00:02:40.635 --> 00:02:44.052
I want to talk about the important stuff.

00:02:50.422 --> 00:02:52.505
I'm talking about important stuff.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:53.763
That's what we should be discussing

00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:56.003
when we're drinking wine.

00:02:56.003 --> 00:02:57.800
Next, people who want to drink wine

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.567
anywhere besides here on my couch.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:03.962
And my friends are always like,
oh, let's go to a wine bar.

00:03:03.962 --> 00:03:07.510
I'm like, for the price of
one glass at the wine bar,

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.053
I could have two bottles here.

00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:11.575
In the privacy of my own home,

00:03:11.575 --> 00:03:13.647
in the comfort of my own couch.

00:03:13.647 --> 00:03:15.372
What's wrong with Hannah's couch?

00:03:15.372 --> 00:03:17.316
Literally I will offer to provide the wine

00:03:17.316 --> 00:03:19.103
if we don't have to go anywhere.

00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:21.758
Or they want to go to a wine tasting.

00:03:21.758 --> 00:03:25.022
I've tasted wine, I know
what wine tastes like.

00:03:25.022 --> 00:03:27.701
Let's get a nice
selection from the bottom.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:28.659
Bleh.

00:03:28.659 --> 00:03:29.992
Let's get a nice selection of wine

00:03:29.992 --> 00:03:32.994
from the bottom shelf of the
grocery store, and taste that.

00:03:32.994 --> 00:03:35.559
Because it all tastes the fucking same.

00:03:35.559 --> 00:03:37.186
♫ I just do what I do

00:03:37.186 --> 00:03:40.535
And last, people who do measly pours.

00:03:40.535 --> 00:03:41.368
'Scuse me.

00:03:42.404 --> 00:03:45.257
They wouldn't make the
wine glasses this big

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:48.095
if you were only supposed
to pour it this full.

00:03:48.095 --> 00:03:50.274
That doesn't make sense.

00:03:50.274 --> 00:03:52.130
I'm not drinking super nice stuff

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:55.034
that needs to, like, aerate
and shit, I don't care.

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:57.685
When you order a beer, they pour the beer

00:03:57.685 --> 00:03:59.818
up to the top rim of the glass

00:03:59.818 --> 00:04:03.007
because they made that glass for the beer.

00:04:03.007 --> 00:04:07.095
So why with wine do they
not do the same thing?

00:04:07.095 --> 00:04:09.810
I want my glass, my full glass of wine,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.964
just like I'd expect a full glass of beer.

00:04:12.964 --> 00:04:15.547
Hey, you want to come fix this?

00:04:17.001 --> 00:04:18.917
They say that a bottle is five glasses.

00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:21.214
I believe that it's two and a half glasses

00:04:21.214 --> 00:04:22.771
if you put your mind to it.

00:04:22.771 --> 00:04:23.971
So, that's all I got for today.

00:04:23.971 --> 00:04:25.751
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom,

00:04:25.751 --> 00:04:27.681
and if there was anything
I missed in this video,

00:04:27.681 --> 00:04:28.782
leave it in the comments.

00:04:28.782 --> 00:04:31.237
What are the worst types
of wine drinkers you know?

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.604
And as always, if you wanna, bleh.

00:04:33.604 --> 00:04:35.820
And as always, if there's a
topic you want me to discuss

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:37.568
in a future episode,
leave it in the comments.

00:04:37.568 --> 00:04:39.528
In the meantime, I'm gonna
finish this glass of wine

00:04:39.528 --> 00:04:41.948
because the ultimate worst
people to drink wine with

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.217
are the people who waste wine.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:46.533
Uh, is it weird if I
pour this into my glass?

00:04:46.533 --> 00:04:47.652
I don't know where you've been,

00:04:47.652 --> 00:04:50.360
but this is perfectly good wine.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.193
Uh.

00:04:51.193 --> 00:04:52.788
Til next time.

00:04:52.788 --> 00:04:55.955
(soft acoustic music)

